@@ -101,6 +101,25 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can push notifications to people's phones and desktops, so that whatever lands in their notification tray reaches them wherever they are.
+Browsers only accept pushes from a server they can identify, so your instance needs its own VAPID key pair.
+You can generate one by running:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm ghcr.io/basecamp/fizzy:main bin/rails push:vapid_keys
+```
+
+Then set the pair it prints:
+
+```sh
+docker run --env VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=abcdef --env VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=123456 ...
+```
+
+Keep the pair stable: changing it invalidates every subscription, and everyone has to turn notifications back on.
+Without it, Fizzy simply won't offer push notifications.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
